\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Fierce raged the tempest o'er the deep,
\par Watch did Thine anxious servants keep,
\par But Thou wast wrapped in guileless sleep,
\par Calm and still.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Save, Lord; we perish! was their cry.
\par Oh, save us in our agony!
\par Thy word above the storm rose high-
\par Peace, be still!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The wild winds hushed, the angry deep
\par Sank like a little child to sleep,
\par The sullen billows ceased to leap,
\par At Thy will.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. So, when our life is clouded o'er,
\par And storm-winds drift us from the shore,
\par Say, lest we sink to rise no more:
\par Peace, be still!
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

